\title{Switch \code{\verb~|bodies~}: beta bodies evaluated without a tabling record}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{machine}
\tag{unreleased}
\tag{performance}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{49fff61}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Under the switch, first named \code{\verb~|m2a~}, the body of a beta step or of an instantiation and the domains and results of a telescope are evaluated without a tabling record, and a body that is a projection of a bound variable becomes a projection of the argument. Measured on top of the step-1 switches with \code{\verb~|probes~}, one worker, native image: CPU -10.5 \% on the Cedar slice, -37.6 \% on reachability, -10.4 \% on Init and -9.8 \% on Std, and the RSS of reachability from 1,136 to 774 MiB. With four workers, median CPU and wall of three interleaved passes: Init 7.47 s and 2.68 s to 6.46 s and 2.48 s, reachability 8.11 s and 4.37 s to 5.24 s and 2.13 s. The wall readings scatter on the loaded host. No difference from the reference engine on the 230 tests and the four corpora. The switch was off when published and joined the default set at the integration of wave 6.}

\p{Detail: [design-switches-document](design-switches-document), [rep-machine-M2](rep-machine-M2). Commit \commit{49fff61}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [evaluation and tabling](design-evaluation-and-tabling), [the switches](design-switches).}
